1
00:00:04,738 --> 00:00:06,208
(Raj:)What are you drawing over there?

2
00:00:06,373 --> 00:00:10,573
(Sheldon:)A hypothetical containment field
for a Frisbee-sized wormhole...

3
00:00:10,744 --> 00:00:13,404
(Sheldon:)...that could serve as a portal
to a parallel universe.

4
00:00:14,047 --> 00:00:16,847
(Howard:)Oh, you silly doodlebug.

5
00:00:18,218 --> 00:00:21,278
(Leonard:)A lot of scientists believe
making contact with other life-forms...

6
00:00:21,454 --> 00:00:23,614
(Leonard:)...would probably not end well for us.

7
00:00:23,823 --> 00:00:25,693
(Sheldon:)It's a Frisbee-sized wormhole, Leonard.

8
00:00:25,859 --> 00:00:28,119
You could block it with a Frisbee.
Calm down.

9
00:00:31,731 --> 00:00:33,791
Do you expect me to build this? Heh.

10
00:00:33,967 --> 00:00:37,197
(Sheldon:)I expect you to wipe the pudding
off your chin. Gentlemen.

11
00:00:39,139 --> 00:00:43,129
(Howard:)Have you guys ever noticed that Sheldon
always disappears every day at 2:45?

12
00:00:43,343 --> 00:00:45,573
- Really?
- He probably just goes to the bathroom.

13
00:00:45,745 --> 00:00:48,545
Actually, no. He goes at 8 a.m.
With optional follow-ups...

14
00:00:48,715 --> 00:00:52,655
...at 1:45 and 7:10 on high-fiber Fridays.

15
00:00:53,787 --> 00:00:55,417
(Raj:)It's sad that you know that.

16
00:00:55,588 --> 00:00:58,458
(Howard:)Oh...
That's just the tip of the sadness iceberg.

17
00:01:00,627 --> 00:01:02,617
(Howard:)I'm looking at his public calendar.

18
00:01:02,796 --> 00:01:05,736
Two-forty-five to 3:05, nothing.

19
00:01:05,899 --> 00:01:08,159
Yesterday, 2:45 to 3:05, nothing.

20
00:01:08,368 --> 00:01:10,928
(Howard:)Last week, nothing. Last month, nothing.

21
00:01:11,104 --> 00:01:13,664
(Howard:)He never has anything booked
during that time.

22
00:01:13,873 --> 00:01:16,673
(Raj:)Twenty minutes a day
completely unaccounted for.

23
00:01:16,876 --> 00:01:20,506
- We should figure out where he goes.
- Ooh, this is exciting.

24
00:01:21,681 --> 00:01:24,511
(Raj:)Like one of my classic
murder-mystery dinner parties.

25
00:01:24,684 --> 00:01:29,814
(Leonard:)Right, the case of who murdered
three Saturday nights of my life.

26
00:01:29,989 --> 00:01:33,289
Colonel Koothrappali in the kitchen
with the olive spread.

27
00:01:34,828 --> 00:01:39,018
(Raj:)It was tapenade and you guys suck.

